    println("║  Theorem 9 (proof) — r-LEVELS OF INDIRECTION                         ║")
    println("║  base pointer O(log⁽ʳ⁾ n) · p₁ = O(log k) · value = k bits           ║")
    println("╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝")
    println("")
    println("The size-class table caps values at one machine word because its class")
    println("slots are sized to the value: a 200-bit value would need a 256-bit")
    println("BASE slot. The paper's chain stores every value 'at the end of a linked")
    println("list of length O(1)': value k bits ← p₁ of O(log k) bits ← … ← base")
    println("pointer of O(log⁽ʳ⁾ n) bits. Phase 15 lifts the v ≤ 64 cap with r = 2")
    println("levels: 128/256-bit values live in the level-1 arena behind a 5-bit")
    println("p₁ (O(log 256)) held in an 8-bit base slot — and the base pointer")
    println("stays 8 bits for EVERY value size, never growing with v.")
    println("")
    println("The r = 3 extension inserts the O(log log k) MIDDLE pointer p₂: values")
    println("up to 2^32 bits flow through base(8) → p₂(6) → p₁(5) → value words.")
    println("The base stays 8 bits even for a 2^32-bit value — the chain's pointer")
    println("widths (8 → 6 → 5) are ALL constant in v; only the word count grows.")
    println("")
}

